BT /F1 10 Tf 50 800 Td 14 TL
(Leave Policy for Shore Staff) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Annual Leave) Tj T*
(Full-time shore staff are entitled to 25 days of paid annual leave per calendar year, in) Tj T*
(addition to public holidays. Part-time staff receive annual leave pro rata to their) Tj T*
(contracted hours. Leave requests must be submitted through the HR portal at least 14 days in) Tj T*
(advance and approved by the line manager. A maximum of 5 days of unused annual leave may be) Tj T*
(carried over into the next calendar year, and carried-over days must be used by 31 March.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Sick Leave) Tj T*
(Employees receive up to 10 days of paid sick leave per calendar year. A medical certificate) Tj T*
(is required for any absence longer than 3 consecutive days. Employees must inform their line) Tj T*
(manager before 10:00 on the first day of absence.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Parental Leave) Tj T*
(Primary caregivers are entitled to 26 weeks of paid parental leave. Secondary caregivers are) Tj T*
(entitled to 4 weeks of paid parental leave, which must be taken within 12 months of the) Tj T*
(birth or adoption. Parental leave must be requested at least 8 weeks before the expected) Tj T*
(start date.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Compassionate Leave) Tj T*
(Employees may take up to 5 days of paid compassionate leave following the death of an) Tj T*
(immediate family member, and up to 2 days for other relatives.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Study Leave) Tj T*
(Employees may take up to 5 days of paid study leave per year to sit approved professional) Tj T*
(examinations. Study leave must be approved by the Head of Department.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. Unpaid Leave) Tj T*
(Unpaid leave of up to 30 days may be granted in exceptional circumstances. Requests for) Tj T*
(unpaid leave are approved by the Head of Department and the HR Business Partner.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
